future-proof your notion exports                            /_/


notion's html export is the only format that keeps
toggles, nested blocks, databases and embeds.
but its pages load images and math from the internet,
sit on a single line and look like plain web pages.

this script makes them offline, editable
and closer to notion's look.


usage:

export as html with everything, subpages and
folders for subpages included, then run:

    $ uv run https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sueszli/notionbackup/refs/heads/main/notionbackup.py export.zip

the result goes to ./export/ next to the zip.
